  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 515.02 Definition of Dug-In Basin",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 515.02 Definition of Dug-In Basin. “Dug-in basin” means an area of privately-owned land excavated to allow inundation by adjacent public waters to access a single public water at a single location along that water’s shoreline.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19; ss by #13124, eff 10-23-20; ss by #14389, eff 9-25-25, EXPIRES: 9-25-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
